<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy | Otter Homecare" description="How Otter Homecare collects, uses and protects your personal information.">
<header class="phero"><div class="wrap"><div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> · About · Privacy Policy</div><h1 style="max-width:22ch">Privacy Policy</h1></div></header><section class="section" style="padding-top:44px"><div class="wrap"><div class="prose"><p class="updated">Last updated: March 2026</p><details class="legal-toc"><summary>On this page</summary><a href="#s1">1. Who we are</a><a href="#s2">2. Data protection contact</a><a href="#s3">3. What we collect</a><a href="#s4">4. How we collect it</a><a href="#s5">5. Lawful bases</a><a href="#s6">6. Who we share with</a><a href="#s7">7. How long we keep it</a><a href="#s8">8. How we keep it secure</a><a href="#s9">9. Your rights</a><a href="#s10">10. Complaints</a><a href="#s11">11. Changes</a><a href="#s12">12. Accessibility</a></details><h2 id="s1">1. Who we are</h2><p>Otter Homecare Limited, First Floor Office Suite 1, Arlington House, 72 Fore Street, Trowbridge, Wiltshire BA14 8HQ. Tel 01225 690022 · <a href='mailto:hello@otterhomecare.co.uk'>hello@otterhomecare.co.uk</a>. We are registered with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO registration <strong>ZB544661</strong>).</p><h2 id="s2">2. Data protection contact</h2><p>Our Data Security and Protection Lead is <strong>James Rowland-Jones, Director</strong>, who can be reached on 01225 690022 for any question about how we handle your personal data.</p><h2 id="s3">3. What personal data we collect</h2><p>Depending on your relationship with us, we may collect:</p><ul><li>People who use our services and their representatives — including contact details, care needs and GP surgery details.</li><li>Staff and applicants — including DBS, payroll and training records.</li><li>Website users and enquirers — name, contact details, and basic usage data (IP, browser).</li></ul><h2 id="s4">4. How we collect personal data</h2><p>Directly from you; from family members or representatives; from healthcare professionals, local authorities and commissioners; via NHS <strong>GP Connect</strong> (with your consent); through our website and digital systems; and through recruitment.</p><h2 id="s5">5. Lawful bases (UK GDPR)</h2><p>We rely on Contract, Legal obligation, Vital interests, Public task, Legitimate interests and Consent. Special category (health) data is processed under Article 9(2)(a) explicit consent and the health/social care conditions in Schedule 1 of the DPA 2018.</p><h2 id="s6">6. Who we share data with</h2><p>Healthcare professionals; local authorities and commissioners; regulators (CQC, safeguarding bodies); IT and software providers; and payroll, HR and professional advisors. With your consent we may write to your GP surgery and access your GP record via GP Connect. <strong>We never sell your data.</strong></p><h2 id="s7">7. How long we keep data</h2><p>We retain personal data only as long as necessary, in line with health and social care records guidance, after which it is securely deleted or anonymised.</p><h2 id="s8">8. How we keep data secure</h2><p>Secure systems, password protection, role-based access, staff training, secure paper storage, compliant IT, and restricted GP Connect access.</p><p>This website also sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and runs no tracking or analytics — see our <a href="/cookies">cookies policy</a> for the plain-English detail.</p><h2 id="s9">9. Your rights</h2><p>You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, and data portability, and to withdraw consent. To exercise any right, contact us using the details above.</p><h2 id="s10">10. Complaints</h2><p>Please contact us first. You also have the right to complain to the ICO at ico.org.uk (helpline 0303 123 1113).</p><h2 id="s11">11. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We review this policy regularly; the latest version is always published on our website.</p><h2 id="s12">12. Accessibility</h2><p>This policy is available in alternative formats on request.</p></div></div></section>
